cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Bounded integrated discrepancy of greedy L2 sequences, with a Lean formalization"
authors:
  - family-names: Denktaş
    given-names: Köksal Berkay
    affiliation: Politecnico di Torino
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9261-1007"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/KoksalBerkay/bounded-integrated-discrepancy"
keywords:
  - discrepancy theory
  - uniform distribution
  - greedy sequences
  - quasi-Monte Carlo
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  Every greedy L2 sequence on [0,1] started from the empty set, in particular
  Kritzinger's sequence, has integrated discrepancy
  G_N(t) = int_0^t (#{k <= N : x_k <= s} - N s) ds bounded by -2/3 <= G_N(t) <= 1/2
  for all N and t. This answers a question of Steinerberger. Consequences include
  |x_1 + ... + x_N - N/2| <= 1/2 and a bound on the quadrature error of every C^2
  function that does not depend on N. All main results are formalised in Lean 4
  with Mathlib.
